    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d455">

                <pb facs="0566" n="498" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg498"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865.857 An 2/76½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic"> President Wilson to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">5 December, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: This is a peremptory
                    note, but I see no other course open to us.</p>
                <p>I understand that Penfield has asked for a fuller statement of the facts from the
                    government at Vienna, but that so far they have not furnished him with any more
                    than we already had. Can we say that we have the Austrian official version of
                    what happened?</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
